# --- arrays: the token (the operands of a copy in its two halves); the names of the data (the cells 1..63: the name in two halves, its width, the previous
# cell with the same hash) and the tree of tables over them (the hash of the name, 12 bits, by parts of 2 bits: 6 levels, a node is 4 entries; the node 1 is the root,
# the nodes 2..255 are taken as a path needs them; an entry holds the next node, at the last level the top cell of the hash; 0 is none)
:tk array 8 8
:sna array 6 56
:snb array 6 56
:swd array 6 20
:scp array 6 6
:trn array 10 8

# --- the character, the state of the reading
:ch data 8 0
:cl data 8 0
:intk data 1 0
:instr data 1 0
:incm data 1 0
:esc data 1 0
:first data 1 1
:pdone data 1 0
